/*
 * Clock distribution unit (CDU) CCF support for Analog
 * Devices ADSP SoCs.
 *
 * Copyright (C) 2026 Analog Devices Inc.
 *
 * The CDU provides the gateable peripheral clocks of the
 * SoC. For each peripheral clock, a CDU mux controls which
 * CGU clock it is to be derived from.
 *
 * The CDU is made up of multiple multiplexers that select
 * clocks generated from the CGU (Clock Generation Unit).
 * After being generated by the CGU, the clocks are divided
 * down via upstream divider clocks and routed to the CDU.
 * Each multiplexer across the CDU has 4 clock input sources
 * (some of which are grounded/not selectable) as well as
 * multiplexer gating functionality.
 *
 * Root clock	    CGU				CDU
 * 		  +------+ ..		+------------------+
 *		  |+---+ | --> CCLK --> | [ ] [x] [ ] [ ]  | --> ARM core
 * SYS_CLKINx --> ||PLL| | ..		| [ ] [ ] [x] [ ]  | --> SHARC core
 *		  |+---+ | --> DCLK --> | [x] [ ] [ ] [ ]  | --> DDR
 *		  |	 | --> SCLK --> | [ ] [ ] [ ] [x]  | --> EMMC
 *		  +------+ ..		+------------------+
 */

